@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed — Link eligibility and viewer generation
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

[*] --> Configured : actual authorized link creation
Configured --> Enabled : explicitly enabled under reviewed policy
Enabled --> Disabled : owner disable / revoke admission
Disabled --> Enabled : explicit permitted re-enable, if supported
Enabled --> Expired : only if expiry policy adopted and reached
Enabled --> Enabled : password rotation / scoped update increments applicable generation
note right of Enabled
 Effective eligibility also requires current resource/content policy.
 Viewer context must match current link authorization generation.
 Download mode change is independent from link enable/disable.
end note
note bottom of Disabled
 Disable/rotation invalidation needs actual synchronized completion boundary.
 Previously emitted/downloaded bytes cannot be recalled.
 Restoring old data must not re-enable revoked links.
end note

@enduml
